<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Data Analytics Process</title>

  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #0f172a, #1e293b, #0f172a);
      color: white;
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 60px 20px;
      font-size: 2.5rem;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: auto;
      position: relative;
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .timeline {
      position: absolute;
      left: 50%;
      width: 4px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
      top: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
    }

    .step {
      width: 50%;
      padding: 20px;
      position: relative;
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(50px);
      transition: all 0.6s ease;
    }

    .step.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    .left {
      left: 0;
      text-align: right;
    }

    .right {
      left: 50%;
    }

    .card {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 20px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    }

    .circle {
      width: 16px;
      height: 16px;
      background: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      position: absolute;
      top: 30px;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .step {
        width: 100%;
        left: 0 !important;
        text-align: left;
      }

      .timeline {
        left: 10px;
      }

      .circle {
        left: 10px;
        transform: none;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

<h1>Data Analytics Process</h1>

<div class="container">
  <div class="timeline"></div>

  <div class="step left">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>1. Define the Research Problem</h3>
      <p>Clearly define objectives, questions, and expected outcomes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step right">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2. Understand Requirements & Plan</h3>
      <p>Determine scope, data needs, stakeholders, and success criteria.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step left">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>3. Data Collection</h3>
      <p>Gather relevant data from surveys, databases, or external sources.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step right">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>4. Data Preparation</h3>
      <p>Clean, transform, and organize the dataset for analysis.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step left">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>5. Exploratory Data Analysis</h3>
      <p>Identify patterns, trends, and anomalies using statistics and visuals.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step right">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>6. Modeling / Analysis</h3>
      <p>Apply statistical or machine learning methods to extract insights.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step left">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>7. Interpretation</h3>
      <p>Translate results into meaningful conclusions and implications.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step right">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>8. Reporting & Visualization</h3>
      <p>Communicate findings through reports, dashboards, and visuals.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step left">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>9. Decision-Making</h3>
      <p>Use insights to support actions and recommendations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step right">
    <div class="circle"></div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>10. Deployment & Monitoring</h3>
      <p>Implement solutions and monitor performance over time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
  const steps = document.querySelectorAll('.step');

  function revealSteps() {
    const triggerBottom = window.innerHeight * 0.85;

    steps.forEach(step => {
      const top = step.getBoundingClientRect().top;

      if (top < triggerBottom) {
        step.classList.add('visible');
      }
    });
  }

  window.addEventListener('scroll', revealSteps);
  revealSteps();
</script>

</body>
</html>
